GIVEN id IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE Provision
`the provision with identifier` MEANS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN p YIELD p's identifier EQUALS id) `the provisions of the text`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN p FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST p

GIVEN id IS A STRING
      heading IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the identifier is indexed and its heading is` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the provision with identifier` id
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST p THEN p's heading EQUALS heading

-- Spot checks, headings copied from the text file.
#ASSERT `the identifier is indexed and its heading is` "1" "Short title"
#ASSERT `the identifier is indexed and its heading is` "18C" "Employer’s individual base superannuation guarantee shortfall for an employee and a QE day"
#ASSERT `the identifier is indexed and its heading is` "59C(2)" "Penalty for failing to pay unpaid superannuation guarantee charge specified in the notice"
#ASSERT `the identifier is indexed and its heading is` "Part 3A" "Choice of fund requirements"
#ASSERT `the identifier is indexed and its heading is` "80" "Regulations"
#ASSERT NOT (`the identifier is indexed and its heading is` "9" "Interpretation")
